# Content model

Business facts live in typed modules under `src/content/`, not in components. A later CMS should be able to replace those modules without a redesign.

- Service definitions, VaultIQ claims, founder wording, and articles each have an explicit status: `draft` or `published`.
- Queries that feed pages return `published` only.
- VaultIQ use cases and feature statements ship as `draft` until someone confirms the product behavior.
- Insights need title, description, category, date, reading time, and status. No article is public without review.
- Do not add case studies, quotes, or client names to fill space.

```ts
// Wrong: a draft essay exported beside published ones with no status
export const essays = [{ title: "Why systems fail" }];

// Right: status is required and pages filter it
export const essays = [
  { slug: "why-systems-fail", status: "draft" as const, title: "Why systems fail" },
];
```

Slot list: `docs/CONTENT_INVENTORY.md`.
